{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/69240-let-s-lateral-thinking-exploit-qualification-thread","id":69240,"title":"Let's Lateral Thinking! (Exploit Qualification Thread)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-10T11:23:56-08:00","id":69240,"title":"Let's Lateral Thinking! (Exploit Qualification Thread)","content":"Given the flexibility of prerequisite Embeds one can use for Exploits, I thought it might be neat to set up a thread for rationales folks could use to qualify for Exploits with given Embeds.<br /> <br /> Format is as follows:<br /> <br /> <b>[Embed Name] &gt; [Exploit Name]</b><br /> Rationale.<br /> <br /> Some examples:<br /> <br /> <b>Authorized &gt; Force Relationship</b><br /> The Embed is keyed off of the relationship humans have with authority - it's easy enough to generalize that to generating reciprocal relationships.<br /> <br /> <b>Alibi &gt; Four Minutes Ago</b><br /> Name aside, &quot;dislocate your Cover&quot; and &quot;I was literally never here&quot; are connected in a straightforward fashion.<br /> <br /> <b>Hesitation &gt; Frozen in Time</b><br /> Expanding the scale of slowdown from single-turn Initiative stalling to multi-turn/multi-minute stopping.<br /> <br /> <b>Sabotage &gt; Raze Infrastructure</b><br /> Almost goes without saying; go from damaging small machines to damaging The Machine.<br /> <br /> If anybody feels like explaining some of the less intuitive sample prerequisites from the book, that's also more than welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T13:00:11-08:00","id":69969,"title":"","content":"This is fun...<br /> <br /> <b>Combustion &gt; Hellfire</b><br /> Gunpowder is totally combustible<br /> <br /> <b>Devil's Advocate &gt; The Word </b><br /> Limited form of suggestion upgrading to a metaphysical control over a person seems to work<br /> <br /> <b>Across a Crowded Room &gt; Affliction</b><br /> Across a Crowded Room's description is stated as being able to cause madness if constant whispering is kept up, and affliction is able to inflict madness<br /> <br /> <b>Like I Built It &gt; Behind the Curtain</b><br /> Not a far stretch to understand a particular piece of Infrastructure and then understand how it's connected to other pieces.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T18:13:08-08:00","id":70204,"title":"","content":"<b>Miles Away &gt; Addictive Presence</b><br /> Uses an internal sound that's comforting to you to come up with a way to make people uncomfortable not being around you.<br /> <br /> <b>Tag and Release &gt; Affliction</b><br /> Common link of &quot;mystically marking a target&quot; - Affliction specifically allows the demon to attach an outward manifestation of the attached Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Voice of the Machine &gt; Extispicy</b><br /> Both hint-gathering powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Without a Trace &gt; Disintegrate</b><br /> From evidence disposal to object disposal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T19:48:48-08:00","id":70245,"title":"","content":"<b>No Quarter &gt; Everybody Hates Him</b><br /> No Quarter causes everybody to go for blood, but what if you redirected all that bloodlust to one person?<br /> <br /> <b>Fungible Knowledge &gt; Reality Enforcement</b><br /> Changing what a character knows how to do, could easily be supercharged into affecting Angels an Demons negatively.<br /> <br /> <b>Occam's Razor &gt; Four Minutes Ago</b><br /> The simplest explanation is usually the correct one right? What's simpler a 8 foot tall unholy monster charging through a wall to kill some poor bastard, or a drunk driver who drove his car through the same wall and ran the guy over?<br /> <br /> <b>Muse &gt; Allies Into Gold</b><br /> I don't know about you guys but if I got hit by a great idea and some guy comes around and tells me to go for it? I'm gonna like him. He does that enough times? I'm looking at my new best friend.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T20:01:33-08:00","id":70247,"title":"","content":"<b>Trust No One &gt; Allies into Gold</b><br /> Understanding and manipulating (by disabling) social structures attached to another individual leads to proficiency in making permanent changes to one's own.<br /> <br /> <b>Fungible Knowledge &gt; Allies into Gold</b><br /> Similar to the above, but the Demon is experienced in manipulating (through a form of metacognition) personal variables in the form of temporary skill transfers, leading to an exploit capable of making changes of a less meta but more permanent manner.<br /> <br /> <b>Momentum &gt; Possession</b> (may be a bit of a stretch)<br /> Learning to make use of others' actions and having it affect one's own (through effects from the other party's successes and failures) inverts at the exploit level, allowing the Demon to instead directly affect another's actions (in a rather dramatic fashion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T20:23:13-08:00","id":70249,"title":"","content":"<b>Everybody Knows &gt; Stalking Horse</b><br /> Both memetic-contact powers that influence the way a person is perceived.<br /> <br /> <b>Like I Built It &gt; Rip the Gates</b><br /> Embed provides knowledge of secret doors and passageways when used in a location.<br /> <br /> <b>Lost in the Crowd &gt; Living Shadow</b><br /> The Exploit specifically can be used to move through the shadows of a crowd of people to move quickly and is further a means of quick disappearance; linking it to a power that allows you to more figuratively vanish into a crowd of people seems sensible.<br /> <br /> <b>Social Dynamics &gt; Force Relationship</b><br /> Leveraging understanding of the relationships within groups to create or alter relationships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T20:57:32-08:00","id":70266,"title":"","content":"<b>Lucky Break &gt; Deep Pockets</b><br /> Ever reach into your pocket and you manage to pull that dollar you didn't think you had for that soda? Well a Demon can do that and more.<br /> <br /> <b>Momentum &gt; Reality Enforcement</b><br /> Once a Demon understands how to manipulate the energy of a given area, it's child's play to prevent a Angel or Demon from accessing their reserves.<br /> <br /> <b>Like I Built It &gt; Animate</b><br /> Understanding how a object is constructed allows a Demon to manipulate her Aether to achieve control.<br /> <br /> <b>Freudian Slip &gt; Everybody Hates Him</b><br /> Ever say something at a party you didn't mean to but it just kinda slipped? Now suddenly no one wants anything to do with you? Yeah, the Demon wanted you to say that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:26:34-08:00","id":70679,"title":"","content":"<b>Across a Crowded Room &gt; Summon</b><br /> Embed can be used to give messages to people from great distances, including &quot;come find me by the end of the day.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Cool Heads Prevail &gt; Halo</b><br /> Calming Embed leads to Exploit with soporific side-effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Fungible Knowledge &gt; Break to Heal</b><br /> Transference of Skill dots shuffled to transference of structural integrity.<br /> <br /> <b>Strike First &gt; Swift Resolution</b><br /> From speedy reactions to speedy completion.<br /> <br /> <b>Voice of the Machine &gt; Inflict Stigmata</b><br /> Draws upon the variant of Omen Sensitivity that stigmatics possess as a link to the patterns Voice of the Machine listens in on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T13:12:57-08:00","id":70808,"title":"","content":"<b>Like I Built It &gt; Disintegrate </b><br /> Understanding an object leads to knowing it's resonant frequency, using her Aether to resonate at that frequency a Demon is able to destroy the object entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Left or Right? &gt; Murder By Improbability </b>(I might be stretching here)<br /> Ever make a turn and then immediately see an accident happen in your review mirror, you think to yourself &quot;Shit! That could have been me!&quot; A demon would have made sure it was you.<br /> <br /> <b>Homogeneous Memory &gt; Everybody Hates Him</b><br /> Make everyone suddenly remember a crime your scapegoat committed that he never did.<br /> <br /> <b>Tower of Babel &gt; Riot</b><br /> Imagine what would happen if people were no longer able to understand each other. Panic? Anger? Fear? Mass hysteria could easily lead to riots in the streets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T15:11:31-08:00","id":70876,"title":"","content":"<b>Alibi &gt; Demon House</b><br /> Compromise-adjusting Embed that dislocates and risks losing your Cover leads into a compromise-adjusting Exploit that disperses and risks losing your Cover.<br /> <br /> <b>Deafen &gt; Solitary Confinement</b><br /> Sensory-deprivation Embed into sensory-deprivation Exploit.<br /> <br /> <b>Occam's Razor &gt; Rain of Blood</b><br /> Exploit that emulates Fortean phenomenon acquired through an Embed that could be used to explain away Fortean phenomena.<br /> <br /> <b>Right Tools, Right Job &gt; Hellfire</b><br /> Tool-enhancement to weapon-enhancement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T16:17:02-08:00","id":70903,"title":"","content":"For the most part I've agreed with a lot of our explanations, but I'm having trouble buying Occam's Razor to Rain of Blood... otherwise we've been doing great","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T18:53:39-08:00","id":70965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pgolasze13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/69240-let-s-lateral-thinking-exploit-qualification-thread?p=70903#post70903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the most part I've agreed with a lot of our explanations, but I'm having trouble buying Occam's Razor to Rain of Blood... otherwise we've been doing great</div> </div> </div> </div>Occam's Razor is a tricky one to begin with, as can be seen by your own example. Not the point of the thread.<br /> <br /> <b>Homogenous Memory &gt; Sermon</b><br /> Both mass mind-altering powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Merciless Gunman &gt; Murder By Improbability</b><br /> Both powers that insta-kill mortals.<br /> <br /> <b>Freudian Slip &gt; Stimulus/Response</b><br /> Both reaction-prompting powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T18:56:51-08:00","id":70966,"title":"","content":"That's true... good job on Merciless Gunman, I hadn't though of Murder by Improbability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T15:33:00-08:00","id":72273,"title":"","content":"<b>Cuckoo's Egg &gt; Hellhounds</b><br /> Swaps living parts for biomechanical ones. Also, commonality of animal names in power names.<br /> <br /> <b>Don't I Know You? &gt; Everybody Hates Him</b><br /> Both powers alter impression levels.<br /> <br /> <b>Earworm &gt; Addictive Presence</b><br /> Can't get the song or the demon out of your head.<br /> <br /> <b>Living Recorder &gt; Hellhounds</b><br /> &quot;Recording&quot; and &quot;downloading&quot; information a Hellhound encounters by granting it Eidetic Memory is specifically given as an example use of the Exploit.<br /> <br /> <b>Lost in the Crowd &gt; Merge</b><br /> Both powers that only work with a group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T16:53:56-08:00","id":72310,"title":"","content":"<b>Identity Theft &gt; Allies Into Gold</b><br /> Why give up your contacts and friends when you can give up an enemies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T17:01:37-08:00","id":72884,"title":"","content":"<b>Cause and Effect &gt; Echoing Death</b><br /> &quot;Take seemingly unrelated action, create desired effect&quot; as a basis for &quot;Take seemingly unrelated action, undo desired effect.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Recurring Hallucinations &gt; Ephemeral Cover</b><br /> Embed curses a victim with visions of things that are not &quot;real&quot; (potentially monsters), Exploit allows the demon to strike and steal the substance of things that are not &quot;real&quot; (specifically monsters).<br /> <br /> <b>Recurring Hallucinations &gt; Solitary Confinement</b><br /> Both terrifying breaking-point inducing powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Someone &gt; Behind the Curtain</b><br /> Effect that locates a nonspecific person that fits a particular criterion leads into effect that moves the demon to nonspecific Infrastructure that fits particular criteria.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T17:42:42-08:00","id":72900,"title":"","content":"This is all very useful to my random demon generator, keep it up, please! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (It was difficult to code the Embed and Exploit coices while having only 'suggested prerequisites' and vague statements that players can justify any Embed as a prerequisite to any Exploit if they wish, and he ST agrees. I went with assuming that means that literally any Embed can be a prerequisite to any Exploit, but weighted towards known prerequisites. This means that there's still quite a lot of strange Embed -&gt; Exploit combinations that ... require some explanation, This thread is gold for supplying reasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T18:25:25-08:00","id":72914,"title":"","content":"<b>Authorized &gt; The Word</b><br /> Both Intimidation-based effects that allow the demon to ensure they are not disturbed.<br /> <br /> <b>Check Backdrop &gt; Living Shadow</b><br /> Shining a light at something makes &quot;backdrop&quot; synonymous with &quot;shadow,&quot; and the Embed makes the former generally safe while the Exploit makes the latter a viable means of transportation.<br /> <br /> <b>Cool Heads Prevail &gt; Riot</b><br /> Decreasing chaos in a group of people changes to increasing chaos in a group of people.<br /> <br /> <b>Cuckoo's Egg &gt; Play on Words</b><br /> Uses the ability to change an object for a comparable one as the basis for changing a word for a comparable one.<br /> <br /> <b>Fulcrum Point &gt; Incendiary</b><br /> From generating sufficient kinetic energy to move any unfixed object to generating sufficient thermal energy to start fires.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T18:43:18-08:00","id":72925,"title":"","content":"<b>Muse &gt; Force Relationship</b><br /> It isn't much of a stretch to go from putting foreign ideas into another's mind to putting whole memories of relationships that never were or using new input thoughts to twist relationships that already exist.<br /> <br /> <b>Combustion &gt; Ephemeral Cover</b><br /> Changing the properties of a material item for one's benefit expands to affecting non-material subjects. It is not so difficult to alter oneself or the properties of an immaterial being for a short time for those skilled in manipulating physical constants.<br /> <br /> <b>Hush &gt; Solitary Confinement</b><br /> An Unchained able to subdue the effects of sound for a particular subject can learn to suffuse further power into the effort and cut off all senses, and indeed the universe's ability to sense, for the unfortunate individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T20:50:01-08:00","id":72986,"title":"","content":"<b>Borrowed Expertise &gt; Inflict Stigmata</b><br /> Go from lending your Skills to &quot;lending&quot; your residual connection to the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> <b>Identity Theft &gt; Possession</b><br /> Identity Theft already makes its namesake more literal than usual; Possession takes the concept to a degree only really exceeded by the invocation of a soul pact.<br /> <br /> <b>Idle Conversation &gt; Sermon</b><br /> The Embed makes it possible to have decidedly unusual conversations in public; the Exploit allows you, arguably, to change a person's definition of &quot;unusual.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Mercury Retrograde &gt; Play on Words</b><br /> Use causing miscommunication to develop deliberate misinterpretation of the spoken word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:34:51-07:00","id":103521,"title":"","content":"<b>Raw Materials &gt; Summon</b><br /> Explicit comparison of the Embed's effect to &quot;summoning&quot; the replacement object.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Someone &gt; Extispicy</b><br /> Leverage your ability to find a person who fits a particular criterion toward more generalized information-gathering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T17:20:45-07:00","id":105196,"title":"","content":"<b>Shift Consequence &gt; Resurrection</b><br /> The boldest sequence of consequence avoidance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T20:58:26-07:00","id":646306,"title":"","content":"I'm glad I came across this thread. I hope my suggestions make sense.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Sabotage &gt; Newton's Nightmares</b><br /> <br /> The sum of the laws of physics could be referred to as a precisely ordered construct or mechanism, except on a much more vast scale. The Embed lets the Demon fiddle with with dials of physical constants, effectively sabotaging a predictable whole in a piecemeal fashion.<br /> <br /> <b>Efficiency and Hesitation &gt; Stop</b><br /> <br /> The former Embed allows the Demon to accomplish more in relation to others, while the latter makes others accomplish less in relation to the Demon. Combine them, and you pretty much described the Exploit.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart's Desire &gt; Addictive Presence</b><br /> <br /> When you figure out what makes people tick, what sets their hearts aflutter and their teeth gritting, it's easy to make them follow you.<br /> <br /> <b>Sabotage and Unperson &gt; Affliction</b><br /> <br /> DNA and environmental factors are intimately interconnected in determining the chances of someone being infected with or developing a disease. Change a few instructions, a chromosome here, some white cells there, and the results can be horrifying. It was only in the last few decades that people with severe and obvious illnesses of body and mind were treated with some dignity. Even so, deformity and infirmity remain a primal fear and tool for intimidation.<br /> <br /> <b>Without A Trace &gt; Behind The Curtain</b><br /> <br /> Utilizing Infrastructure in this relatively direct way requires one to constantly watch their steps and footprints. One can never be too methodical when &quot;borrowing&quot; the tools of the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> <b>Occam's Razor &gt; Context Matters</b><br /> <br /> You would be surprised by how many weird and suspicious events you can explain by sounding confident and rational in front of scared and uninformed people. This goes doubly so for the supernatural denizens of the NWOD, and triply so for Demons.<br /> <br /> <b>Wave Function Collapse &gt; Decoy</b><br /> <br /> This Embed allows Demons to mess with with the quantum states of other Demons, and it gives way to the &quot;Terrible Avatar&quot; and &quot;Reality Reinforcement&quot; Exploits. Decoy seemed like a good candidate for a trifecta of Exploits that mess with the true forms of the God-Machine's creations.<br /> <br /> <b>Victory At Any Cost &gt; Extispicy</b><br /> <br /> Well, duh. You would have to be pretty damn desperate to rip someone's guts out for information about the future that may turn out to be false or even dangerous.<br /> <br /> <b>Knock-Off &gt; Ephemeral Cover</b><br /> <br /> If it looks a Spirit, talks like a Spirit, and phases through matter like a Spirit, not many would say it's a Demon pulling a clever trick.<br /> <br /> <b>Cause And Effect &gt; Eye For An Eye</b><br /> <br /> You mess with my Ring or my Cultists, you mess with me.<br /> <br /> <b>Raw Materials &gt; Rain Of Blood</b><br /> <br /> The Embed renders one object useless to bring a desired object to you. It could be said that this Embed's occult subroutines also allow a space-time distortion that swaps the coordinates of a section in the atmosphere with several other coordinates where the desired materials are present.<br /> <br /> <b>Don't I Know You? &gt; Show Of Power</b><br /> <br /> Yes, I am most definitely one of the Dark Mother's offspring and not a pod person at all. You shouldn't accuse family like that, it is very rude.<br /> <br /> <b>Sum Of All Fears &gt; Stalking Horse</b><br /> <br /> For a time beyond time, when we huddled in caves and had no names for the things the dark, banishment meant death. Even now, ostracism and the resulting isolation make you easy pickings for the monsters, even if you are armed to the teeth.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Someone &gt; Summon</b><br /> <br /> This Embed helps the Demon narrow down the innumerable criteria for identifying subjects until he has all the necessary details for bringing just the right person to him and move his plans along.<br /> <br /> <b>Alibi &gt; Two Places At Once</b><br /> <br /> I am very surprised that this connection isn't in the book. It is the same principle of occult physics, but applied to a pair of locations instead of the Demon himself.<br /> <br /> <b>The Look &gt; Ultimatum</b><br /> <br /> The Embed allows the Demon to restrict the number of states the perceived target can be in, but it only restricts bodily functions like movement and breathing. By applying a much greater concentration and complex bending of constants that make up who the target is, the restrictions need not be focused on biochemical reactions.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Message and Muse &gt; Visions Of Heaven And Hell</b><br /> <br /> Both Embeds alter the perceptions and thought patterns of a target in a way that is customized to control him to a stronger degree. The Exploit does the same, but alters both the path of electricity in the nervous system and the less concrete mechanisms of the intangible mind.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-31-2015, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T00:55:53-07:00","id":646428,"title":"","content":"<b>Momentum &gt; Animate</b><br /> <br /> Both fundamentally involve making use of an outside energy to increase the energy output of a subject. The only real difference is in the receiver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T09:54:36-07:00","id":646906,"title":"","content":"One I've used just recently in a game:<br /> <br /> <b>Freeze Assets</b> \u27a4 <b>Stop</b><br /> The victim finds himself moving in an environment where liquid assets freeze and cannot be manipulated. The demon understands that liquid assets, like bank accounts and credit balances, are not bound to material correspondents. They are measured in opportunity, not volume. In this way, the demon recognizes also: time is money.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}